Repo: /Users/marcel.a.n.navarro/Dev/zimmermann-pwa. Branch: feature/SFCC-91_pdp-colour-swatches. This is a narrow rework round. Do not stage, do not commit. Do NOT use `git stash` under any circumstances. Touch only `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmColourSwatch/index.test.tsx` — no other file.

A prior fix added `position: 'relative'` and `zIndex: 1` inside `zimmColourSwatchGroup.css.ts`'s... no wait — inside `zimmColourSwatch.css.ts`'s `_focusVisible` block (fixing a real bug where a focused swatch's outline had its right edge covered by the next zero-gap sibling). That fix shipped without a regression test, on the mistaken belief that jsdom can't observe `:focus-visible`-scoped styles at all. A reviewer independently proved that belief wrong for `position`/`zIndex` specifically (jsdom's `getComputedStyle` DOES reflect these correctly once a real `.focus()` call happens — only `outline`/`outlineOffset` themselves are a separate, genuine jsdom limitation, unrelated to this fix).

Add exactly this test to `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmColourSwatch/index.test.tsx` (already validated by the reviewer to discriminate correctly — fails without the fix, passes with it — adapt only the import names/paths if this file's existing tests use slightly different ones, check the top of the file first for the real import names for `ChakraProvider`, `theme`, `MemoryRouter`, `ZimmTokensGlobal`, and the existing `IMAGE_URL`-equivalent constant):

```tsx
test('focus-visible position/zIndex are not hidden by the next sibling swatch (regression guard, SFCC-91)', () => {
  const { container } = render(
    <ChakraProvider theme={theme}>
      <MemoryRouter>
        <ZimmTokensGlobal />
        <div style={{ display: 'flex', gap: 0 }}>
          <ZimmColourSwatch name="Bay Blue" imageUrl={IMAGE_URL} isSelected={false} isFocusable={true} />
          <ZimmColourSwatch name="Ivory" imageUrl={IMAGE_URL} isSelected={false} isFocusable={true} />
        </div>
      </MemoryRouter>
    </ChakraProvider>,
  );
  const first = container.querySelectorAll('[data-testid="colour-swatch"]')[0] as HTMLElement;
  first.focus();
  const cs = getComputedStyle(first);
  expect(cs.position).toBe('relative');
  expect(cs.zIndex).toBe('1');
});
```

Add a comment above it noting that `position`/`zIndex` are confirmed observable in this project's jsdom setup even though `outline`/`outlineOffset` are not (a separate, pre-existing jsdom limitation) — so a reader doesn't wonder why this test only checks two of the four `_focusVisible` properties.

Check the existing test file's actual constant name for the placeholder image URL (it's referenced as `IMAGE_URL` above but confirm the real name used elsewhere in the file) and use whatever the file already uses, don't introduce a second differently-named constant for the same thing.

Place this test inside the existing `describe('ZimmColourSwatch', ...)` block, alongside the other tests, in whatever position reads most naturally (e.g. near the other `isSelected`/`isFocusable` tests, since it's testing a related but distinct concern).

## Verification — run yourself, report exact output

```
npx tsc --noEmit
npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/atoms/zimmColourSwatch/index.test.tsx
npm run test
node scripts/auditTokenUsage.mjs
```

Confirm the new test passes. Confirm the full atom test file now shows 9 tests (8 existing + 1 new), all passing. Confirm `npm run lint` still shows the same pre-existing baseline (20 problems, none in this file). Report the exact pass/fail output — do not just say "passed."

Also, as a genuine mutation check (not because you need to re-derive the fix, just to prove this specific test is real): temporarily comment out or remove the `position: 'relative'` and `zIndex: 1` lines from `zimmColourSwatch.css.ts` (the ALREADY-FIXED file, not something you're re-implementing — just temporarily reverting it to confirm your new test catches the regression), re-run your new test, confirm it FAILS, then restore those two lines exactly as they were and confirm it passes again. Report both outputs. Do not leave the recipe file modified at the end — only `index.test.tsx` should show as changed when you're done.

